WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.520
If you want to hear how the original 1933
Invisible Man secretly appears in this

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.200
2020 reimagining then stick around to the
end of this video.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.440
Oh, yeah I'm over here.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:19.160
Our story begins at 3:42 in the morning as
Cecillia wakes up to try to escape from Adrian's

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.160
prison like estate.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.490
One of the first things she does is turn his
security camera towards the bedroom, so that

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.960
she can keep an eye on him rather than the
other way around.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.470
I think it's kind of interesting how she has
this strategy of using Adrian's technology

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:33.050
against him from the very beginning, and it
isn't until later until she realizes how to

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.800
fully take advantage of that idea.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.400
Two weeks after escaping she is still super
paranoid...

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.440
and at that point we don't know why.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.500
We don't know that Adrian was this optics
technology mastermind.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.320
But there are clues, like Cecillia painting
over her webcam, the mechanical sounds she

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.719
hears at night, and later, flashes of light,
which we find out to be Adrian taking photos

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.880
of her, part of his plan to make her go crazy.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.079
She also receives the mail, which informs
her of Adrian's will reading at an address

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:01.600
that nobody is supposed to know that she's at,
which doesn't make sense until we find out

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.030
that Adrian is using the suit to stalk her.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:07.979
Adrian's full name by the way is Adrian Griffin,
which is a slight nod to Jack Griffin, the

00:01:07.979 --> 00:01:11.420
scientist who learned how to make himself
invisible and became the original Invisible

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.280
Man.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.260
Cecilia's name on the other hand, is a feminine
version of the name Cecil, which is derived

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.590
from the Latin word meaning blind...

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.659
seeing as how she can't see Adrian.

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:24.060
There are also a lot of examples of the camera
angle suddenly cutting to a wide shot taken

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.649
from another room, and I think this is supposed
to be Adrian's point of view as he's sneaking

00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:29.490
around the house and spying on her.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.789
And one more note of those mechanical sounds
that she hears.

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:35.649
The Invisible Man doesn't have a signature
sound like some of the other classic Universal

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:36.460
monsters.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.619
I mean, you can't have him growl like the
Wolfman or hiss like Dracula, cause that would

00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:43.319
be ridiculous, so it's cool how they found
a sound that fits the sci-fi reimagining of

00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:45.499
the story and is also still really creepy.

00:01:45.499 --> 00:01:49.539
When Cecillia is escaping we see her Cal Poly
Architecture sweater, and later she interviews

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:51.399
for a job at an architectural firm.

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:54.609
The characters have fitting career choices
for their roles in the story.

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:58.109
Architecture represents privacy; it's the
idea of putting up walls and shielding yourself

00:01:58.109 --> 00:01:59.679
from the gaze of the outside world.

00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:03.679
And optics technology represents an invasion
of privacy, people like Adrian are the suppliers

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:08.069
for paparazzi, and in our world today technology
companies are seen as leeches for data and

00:02:08.069 --> 00:02:10.950
are often criticized for their misleading
privacy policies.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:14.459
So there's some social commentary going on
here, which, if you're gonna remake a classic

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:17.599
movie and bring it into modern times, it's
always nice to see that there's actually a

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:19.129
reason for that update.

00:02:19.129 --> 00:02:22.569
After Cecillia escapes, she's staying at James's
house, and I noticed him wearing a shirt that

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:24.709
says Prestige Records, 1949.

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:28.379
The year may be a reference to the release
day of The Invisible Man Appears, which was

00:02:28.379 --> 00:02:32.319
a Japanese adaptation of HG Wells's novel,
The Invisible Man, which is what the original

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.540
film is based on.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.290
It's also a Japanese restaurant where Cecillia
and Emily later have their reconciliation

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.670
meeting, though that may be a coincidence.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.480
Hard to say for sure.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.500
"Hahahahaha."

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.100
"AH!"

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:01.300
But there's a bigger reference to the original
Invisible Man nested inside of James's house.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:04.790
Cecilia is sleeping in the same room as the
daughter Sydney, and her dream is to go to

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:08.090
fashion school, so her room is filled with
clothing of her own design.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.450
As you might expect, there's a mannequin in
the room, and it's wearing this one hat...

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.099
and if I remember correctly it's wearing sunglasses
too.

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:17.640
This is a big easter egg, because the mannequin
is basically dressed up like The Invisible

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.310
Man from the original movie.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:22.670
It actually kind of confused me when I first
saw it on screen, because I thought we were

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.579
seeing the monster for the first time, and
it took me a minute to realize that it was

00:03:25.579 --> 00:03:26.760
an actual mannequin.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.780
I'm sure most audiences who aren't familiar
with the 1933 film didn't have that issue

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.280
though.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.460
There would be another big reference to the
that original movie later, but in the meantime,

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.680
there were some more contemporary references
as well.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.260
The blanket pulling scene pays homage to The
Conjuring...

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.379
...and when Cecillia spreads coffee beans
all over the floor to try to catch the invisible

00:03:50.379 --> 00:03:54.969
man's footsteps, it's very reminiscent of Paranormal Activity,
where the character Katie spreads flour on

00:03:54.969 --> 00:03:57.600
the floor to try to record the invisible entity's
footsteps.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.260
"There's footsteps in, but no footsteps out..."

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.580
"Oh God!"

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.900
I think that the director of The Invisible
Man, Leigh Whannell put in these connections

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.019
in because he's friends with James Wan, who
directed The Conjuring and Oren Peli who directed

00:04:17.019 --> 00:04:18.019
Paranormal Activity.

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:22.400
In fact, Whannell's directorial debut was
Insidious: Chapter 3, (excellent movie) and

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.590
that film was produced by Wan and Peli.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:28.169
Adrian messes with Cecilia's life and makes
her question her own sanity.

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:31.630
Things really get crazy when he drugs her
and she passes out during her job interview.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.150
She ends up in the hospital, and in the hallway
there's another patient who is completely

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:38.840
wrapped up in bandages, which is a clever
reference to, once again, the original Invisible

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.750
Man where he hides his invisibility by entirely
wrapping himself up in bandages.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.100
The scene where he reveals himself...

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.100
Or...

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.770
I guess does the opposite of that... shows
himself removing these bandages and is considered

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.380
to be the most iconic scene in the movie.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:53.650
"I'll show you who I am... and what I am!

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:57.580
Hoohoo hahahah!"

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.080
"Look, he's all eaten away."

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:08.400
"How do you like that, eh?"

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.590
After Cecilia confirms that Adrian is stalking
her by finding the phone, knife, and photographs

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:17.180
in the attic, she goes back to Adrian's fortress
of a house and strangely, the dog is still

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.960
there, another clue that he's still living
there.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.990
I imagine when he faked his suicide, he left
the dog to the brother as not to raise suspicion,

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.460
and then had him returned him to the house,
where nobody would find out he's still living

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.990
there because of the huge walls that surround
the place.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:32.460
Speaking of the brother, let's fast-forward
a little bit to when Cecilia's in the psych

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:35.169
ward after being framed for killing her sister
by Adrian.

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:38.449
His brother informs Cecilia that he'll be
withholding the money from the will because

00:05:38.449 --> 00:05:42.330
she committed a crime, and she basically figures
out that he's in on the whole operation.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:45.440
She calls him a jellyfish version of Adrian,
because he has no spine.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.490
"BECAUSE I'VE SEEN MORE SPINE IN JELLYFISH!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.830
SEEN MORE GUTS IN 11 YEAR OLD KIDS!"

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.220
No, but ok.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.139
Maybe it's just my Emo Abraham Lincoln side
showing, but the more I think about it, the

00:05:56.139 --> 00:05:59.530
more that I actually think this could be a
reference to that song by Brand New.

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:00.530
I mean think about it.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.979
The main chorus of the song is "everyone's
caught onto everything you do."

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:08.820
"Everyone's caught onto everything you do."

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:13.360
Adrian has manipulated Cecillia for a long
time, but nobody knew the extent of how badly

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.099
he controlled her until she escaped and exposed
his behaviour.

00:06:16.099 --> 00:06:19.629
Then there’s also that line: “Don't apologize
(I hope you choke and die!)”.

00:06:19.629 --> 00:06:22.750
"Don't apologize (I hope you choke and die!)"

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.819
...and at the end of the movie, Adrian tries
to make up with her and she ends up using

00:06:25.819 --> 00:06:29.409
the invisibility suit to cut his throat, he
chokes and dies.

00:06:29.409 --> 00:06:30.409
So there’s that.

00:06:30.409 --> 00:06:34.169
Leigh Whannell is from Australia so I don’t
know how familiar he would be with the Long

00:06:34.169 --> 00:06:38.560
Island emo scene but one thing he’s probably
familiar with is aquatic life, because Australia

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.900
is regarded as the world’s top scuba destination.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.280
I noticed later on in the movie, that Sydney
has a jellyfish shirt.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.160
And that got me thinking again about Cecilia
calling Adrian’s brother a jellyfish.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:51.040
In Australia, there’s a creature known as
the Irukandji Jellyfish, and they’re considered

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:54.760
dangerous because they’re venomous and they
can make themselves invisible, or at least

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.120
very close to invisible.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.710
And this fits perfectly because Adrian’s
brother is later discovered to also be using

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.080
the invisibility suit to help Adrian with
his scheme.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.080
"Honey!"

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.080
"What?"

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.600
"Where's my super suit?"

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:08.190
He’s a toxic person with the ability to
go invisible.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:12.010
In this case, instead of divers off the coast
being the victims, it’s a seemingly endless

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:15.690
amount of cops, who just seem to keep spawning
and getting killed in that one hallway.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.380
"What's going on over here?

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:20.980
What are they in the roof?

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:23.370
How you gonna spawn inside the roof?

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:24.370
Yeah.."

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:29.270
So the story ends with, as I mentioned, Cecillia
killing Adrian, claiming it wasn’t her,

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:32.729
and getting James to go along with her story…
somewhat reluctantly.

00:07:32.729 --> 00:07:36.410
She steals the invisibility suit for herself,
cause I guess these things have really good

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:40.280
battery life, and in doing so seems to set
up the sequel, The Invisible Woman.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:43.699
I’m guessing she is gonna start using the
suit for herself, and slowly start to become

00:07:43.699 --> 00:07:46.270
the villain, and James is going to be the
one to have to try to stop her.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.270
And I’m all for it.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:50.099
I think there’s a lot more that can be covered
with this concept; and with smart characters

00:07:50.099 --> 00:07:51.909
like these, it should be a lot of fun.

00:07:51.909 --> 00:07:55.719
Of course, I’ll be covering it here on CZsWorld
if that does happen, but until then, click

00:07:55.719 --> 00:07:56.900
the video on the left

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:01.009
And go ahead and subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week, ring that deathbell

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:03.639
for notifications and I’ll see you in the
next one.

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:06.280
Assuming we both survive.

